# Judging Notes - [SoilSat]

## 1. Impact
Soil degradation happens slowly it is invisible. It can be devastating. 
Soil Memory shows this problem by converting raw NASA satellite data into soil health histories. 
It allows farmers to try crop rotation plans on a screen before they plant a single seed in the ground.

## 2. Creativity
Existing tools give a real-time snapshot, while Soil Memory gives foresight. We reconstruct a 10-year soil memory profile 
to let farmers simulate how different crop rotations would perform against actual historical climate stress before planting.

## 3. Product
A live, functional Streamlit web app built directly on top of Google Earth Engine and NASA Earthdata.
A farmer draws or selects their field, and the app instantly pulls real MODIS and SMAP data to visualize the land's 10-year soil 
timeline—letting them run side-by-side rotation scenarios on actual satellite history.

## 4. Sustainability
Built entirely on free, open-source tools and free NASA data, Soil Memory can be improved and forked by anyone. 
The tool stays free for individual farmers, only institutions would pay. 
Expansion would go through trusted intermediaries like agricultural extension agents,
with multi-language support and offline-friendly PDF exports planned.

## 5. Presentation
We skip the technical jargon and tell a human story through "Farmer Dalal." 
We show her fighting an invisible problem—dwindling soil health—and hand her a visible solution. 
Built around a crisp live dashboard demo backed up by a pre-recorded backup video,
our pitch proves that space-grade data can solve real-world problems on the ground.
